
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Timothy Williamson will be the inaugural speaker in a new lecture series accompanying a new journal: <em><a href="https://academic.oup.com/cjp?" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The Chinese Journal of Philosophy</a></em> (CJP). </p>



<span id="more-27636"></span>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="651" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture-1024x651.jpg" alt="" class="wp-image-27637" style="aspect-ratio:1.5730000299733238;width:651px;height:auto" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture-1024x651.jpg 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture-300x191.jpg 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture-768x488.jpg 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture-250x159.jpg 250w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-journal-of-philosophy-lecture.jpg 1454w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Published by Oxford University Press, the CJP is an open-access (including no cost to authors) general philosophy journal.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It is edited by Roger T. Ames (Hawaii), Wei Cheng (Peking), Nicolas De Warren (Penn State), Sebastian Sunday Grève (Peking), and You Zhao (Peking). </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The journal is open to submissions &#8220;from anyone working in philosophy and on all philosophical topics.&#8221; According to its <a href="https://academic.oup.com/cjp?" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">website</a>, </p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>the journal aims to represent the multitude of topics and approaches that may fall under the heading of ‘philosophy’ in the world today, with a special focus on philosophical research that has the potential to make different traditions of thought more fruitful for one another.</em></p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That is to say, it is not a journal primarily about Chinese philosophy, anymore than the <em>Canadian Journal of Philosophy</em> is a journal about Canadian philosophy, or the <em>Australasian Journal of Philosophy </em>is about Australasian philosophy . The <a href="https://phil.pku.edu.cn/xzqk/cjp/intro.htm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">note</a>, &#8220;like these other journals, the <em>Chinese Journal of Philosophy</em> originates in a particular region whilst editing and publishing as an international collective, operating in English, and promoting work from around the world.&#8221;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">CJP is currently open for submissions and plans to begin publishing articles in April. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The launch of the journal includes the start of a new lecture series from the <a href="https://phil.pku.edu.cn/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Department of Philosophy and Religious Studies at Peking University</a>. Williamson&#8217;s inaugural lecture is this Wednesday, and will be delivered in person and <a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/j/86727223234" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">online</a>. </p>



